-- title:
--   Integral norm-string lift of diagonal units at unramified places
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L/K$ a Galois extension, and let $\sigma \in \operatorname{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $\tau \in \operatorname{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$ and assume that every height-one prime $w'$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ whose contraction to $\mathcal{O}_K$ is $v$ satisfies $\mathrm{ramificationIdx'}(v, w') = 1$, i.e. $v$ is unramified in $L$. Let $x, y$ be units of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_{K_v}$ of the completion $K_v =$ `v.adicCompletion K`. Then there exist units $d_1, d_2$ of $L \otimes_K K_v$ such that the diagonal element $\mathrm{diag}(d_1, d_2) \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ (with the evident inverse $\mathrm{diag}(d_1^{-1}, d_2^{-1})$) lies in [`AutomorphicForm.semiLocalIntegralSet K L v`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L136), meaning that all entries of both $\mathrm{diag}(d_1,d_2)$ and its inverse lie in the image of `HeightOneSpectrum.tensorAdicCompletionIntegersTo K L (𝓞 L) v`, and such that the norm string $$\prod_{i=0}^{[L:K]-1} \sigma^i\bigl(\mathrm{diag}(d_1,d_2)\bigr),$$ the ordered product of the iterates of the map induced entrywise by $\sigma$ on $L \otimes_K K_v$, equals the image of $\mathrm{diag}(x, y) \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ (entries the images of $x$ and $y$ in $K_v$) under the base-change homomorphism $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ induced by $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$.
--
--   This is the local exactness statement underlying base change at an unramified place: a diagonal element of the unit torus of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ is hit exactly, not merely up to a unit, by the twisted norm (norm string) of a semi-locally integral diagonal element of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$. It rests on surjectivity of the norm on local units in the unramified case together with the computation of the norm string of a diagonal matrix, and it feeds the construction of twisted torus families as restricted-product elements in the comparison of hyperbolic terms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_exists_diagUnits2_mem_semiLocalIntegralSet_and_normString_eq_toTensorGL_of_ramificationIdx_eq_one.lean

import Definitions.Def_AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital
